[{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"CurrentModule = PiecewiseVanillaModel","category":"page"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for PiecewiseVanillaModel.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Modules = [PiecewiseVanillaModel]","category":"page"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel._d_1-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel._d_1","text":"_d_1(strike, forward, nu)\n\nCalculate the Black formula d_1 term.\n\nWe implement this once in order to fine-tune corner cases later.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_implied_stdev_numeric","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_implied_stdev_numeric","text":"bachelier_implied_stdev(price, strike, forward, call_put, min_max = (1.0e-4, 6.0e-2))\n\nCalculate the implied normal standard deviation ν from a Bachelier model price.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_implied_volatility_numeric","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_implied_volatility_numeric","text":"bachelier_implied_volatility(price, strike, forward, T, call_put, min_max = (0.0001, 0.02))\n\nCalculate the implied normal volatility σ from a Bachelier model price.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_price-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_price","text":"bachelier_price(strike, forward, nu, call_put)\n\nCalculate Vanilla option price V in Bachelier model.\n\nArgument strike (K) represents the option strike, forward (F) is the forward price of the underlying S, i.e. F = ES(T) in the respective pricing measure.\n\nArgument nu represents the standard deviation of the forward price. For annualised normal volatility σ, we have ν = σ √T. Finally, call_put is the call (+1) or put (-1) option flag.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_price-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_price","text":"bachelier_price(strike, forward, σ, T, call_put)\n\nCalculate Vanilla option price V in Bachelier model with volatility parameter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_vega-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_vega","text":"bachelier_vega(strike, forward, σ, T)\n\nCalculate Vanilla option Vega in Bachelier model with volatility parameter.\n\nHere, Vega is calculated as dV  dσ.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_vega-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.bachelier_vega","text":"bachelier_vega(strike, forward, nu)\n\nCalculate Vanilla option Vega in Bachelier model.\n\nHere, Vega is calculated as dV  d ν.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.black_price-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.black_price","text":"black_price(strike, forward, nu, call_put)\n\nCalculate Vanilla option price V in Black model.\n\nArgument strike (K) represents the option strike, forward (F) is the forward price of the underlying S, i.e. F = ES(T) in the respective pricing measure.\n\nArgument nu represents the standard deviation of the forward price. For annualised lognormal volatility σ, we have ν = σ T. Finally, call_put is the call (+1) or put (-1) option flag.\n\nWe allow broadcasting for arguments.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#PiecewiseVanillaModel.black_price-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"Home","title":"PiecewiseVanillaModel.black_price","text":"black_price(strike, forward, σ, T, call_put)\n\nCalculate Vanilla option price V in Black model with volatility parameter.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"}]
